WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:10.200
The last time America created a new
military service was in 1947, when the

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:13.830
Air Force split off from the Army.
Seventy years later, the House of

00:00:13.830 --> 00:00:18.390
Representatives has asked the Air Force
to reorganize and spin-off a new Space

00:00:18.390 --> 00:00:22.289
Corps. But the result would not be akin
to the relationship between the Navy and

00:00:22.289 --> 00:00:26.820
the Marines, as its supporters suggest.
That's because Congress would leave the

00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:30.779
Space Corps with little beyond
navigation, GPS, and communication

00:00:30.779 --> 00:00:34.829
satellites. It would not oversee vital
space operations including nuclear

00:00:34.829 --> 00:00:40.050
strike, ballistic missile defense, or
anti-satellite missions. This "new" service

00:00:40.050 --> 00:00:44.489
would be less "Space Corps" and more of a
"satellite force". The White House, Air

00:00:44.489 --> 00:00:48.270
Force leadership, and the Secretary of
Defense have all spoken out against the

00:00:48.270 --> 00:00:52.140
plan, and it's easy to see why: While it's
been touted as a way to compel the Air

00:00:52.140 --> 00:00:55.860
Force to focus on space, all it would
really do is create more Pentagon

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:59.640
bureaucracy. Instead, it's best for
Congress to work with the Air Force to

00:00:59.640 --> 00:01:03.809
strengthen our existing Space Command.
Let's keep America's Space Marines

00:01:03.809 --> 00:01:05.700
relegated to science fiction.

